WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:06.640
Today we're going to explore what happens

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:10.540
when Edge Computing meets 3 distinct industries.

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:14.380
This is "The Future of".

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.560
Today, I'm going to be talking to Dr. Luca Marchi,

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.150
an expert and leader in the retail industry.

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:23.160
So, Luca, thanks for joining me here today.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:25.300
What do you think is going to be

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:29.010
the opportunity to transform the retail industry

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:30.500
with the introduction of Edge Computing?

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:33.980
Retailers, they gather a lot of data about their consumer,

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:35.840
both internal and external,

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.180
but the main touch point is the cashier,

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:40.980
what you bought, at what price and when,

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.960
how frequently you buy it.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.410
But think about how many different products you look at

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:47.600
in a supermarket.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.340
All those things are not really captured.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:54.710
So, you can use smart devices in different areas of a store

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:56.850
and collect those touch points

00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:00.710
and understand more deeply your customer behavior.

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:04.270
So, really, the benefit of Edge Computing

00:01:04.270 --> 00:01:05.810
in the future of retail

00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:08.440
is really going to come from the power of personalization.

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:09.600
Yeah, I totally agree.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:13.390
Personalization is going to be so important.

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:14.970
You need to sell to everybody,

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:18.800
but with very different and specific customer experience.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:21.120
So, what do you find most exciting about

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.470
this emerging world of Edge Computing

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:25.110
in the retail industry?

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:26.743
Well, I believe there are 3 things

00:01:26.743 --> 00:01:28.060
that are super exciting.

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:31.140
The first one, it could be the fully automated store.

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:35.260
The second one is the ability to leverage data

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:37.820
that is not generated in the store.

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:42.050
And the third one is a complete immersive experience,

00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:46.230
characterized by virtual reality, or augmented reality.

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:47.820
Which kind of brings us back to, then,

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:51.570
the other part of the equation for the retailers,

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:53.320
and the pressure that they're under economically

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:54.960
is how to do so,

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.920
how to introduce these capabilities at lower cost.

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:01.250
So, Edge also has the great advantage of the Cloud,

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:03.730
of being flexible and scalable.

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:06.790
These really helps the cost-effectiveness

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:10.300
of integrating and deploying an Edge network.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:12.700
Also, the maintenance costs are very limited,

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:15.290
because you can still manage them centrally,

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:18.640
but you are able to deploy different software

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:21.310
according to the different situation.

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:23.293
So, Luca, I really wanna thank you for being here today.

00:02:23.293 --> 00:02:24.930
It's going to be exciting,

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:27.340
and I'm glad to have you here on board with us,

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:28.840
to take us through that journey.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:33.260
Val, welcome, here.

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:35.260
Thank you for bringing your expertise

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:37.410
in the area of Financial Services.

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:39.700
What does Edge Computing mean

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:41.830
to the financial services industry?

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:45.070
With Edge Computing we're able to go that next step

00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:48.110
of engagement with consumers anywhere, anytime.

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:49.550
So, we have ATMs.

00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:51.510
In the ATM environment currently today

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:52.430
there are cameras.

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:54.210
We want to make sure it's a safe environment.

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:57.640
But also, in the situation where there is fraud,

00:02:57.640 --> 00:02:58.900
they have the data collected

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:01.410
to be able to, you know, look at the log files

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:02.560
and see what happens.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:04.910
That's all post-event, though.

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:06.300
So, what we can do now is,

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:10.210
in real time, identify that we have a risk,

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:13.030
either to human safety or to fraudulent behavior.

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:16.550
And, with that, alert within financial markets,

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:17.720
for example, and trading.

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:18.840
Your decisions have to be made

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:21.310
so rapidly in that environment.

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:22.510
And, you know, the latency,

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:24.300
network bandwidth, and sending things to the Cloud

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:25.133
to make it such -

00:03:25.133 --> 00:03:26.320
it's just, it's prohibitive

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:29.297
to the ability to bring those analytics

00:03:29.297 --> 00:03:31.360
right down to the Edge, where the data's created

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:32.193
at the network,

00:03:32.193 --> 00:03:36.010
and then alert for decision-making in milliseconds,

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:38.410
can be a huge differentiator in gains.

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:41.000
To me, it's a very exciting time in our industry.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.790
Well, Val, thank you so much for being here today.

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:45.840
Thank you for your insight, your expertise.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:51.120
So, Utpal, I want to thank you so much for being here today.

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.340
So let's talk a little bit about

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:54.050
the distinction between 5G and Edge,

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:56.850
because we use them interchangeably sometimes,

00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:58.750
but in fact they're quite different, aren't they?

00:03:58.750 --> 00:03:59.670
Absolutely.

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:04.320
So, Edge use-case can also be done in 4G.

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:06.700
Edge is independent of 5G.

00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:11.440
But 5G will provide a whole new set of opportunities

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:15.500
or use-cases that never existed in a 4G environment.

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:17.940
A classic example would be a use-case

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:22.400
which existed in 4G, but it may not have those latency,

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:25.030
may not have those network slicing features,

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:26.570
may not have those bandwidths,

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:29.460
and so its ability to be powerful,

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:31.820
or impactful, would be limited.

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:34.500
5G will transform it.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:36.420
5G is the fuel for Edge computing.

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:37.253
Absolutely.

00:04:37.253 --> 00:04:38.930
That's a right way of putting it.

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:41.960
If I'm a CIO for a telco (telecommunications company),

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:45.620
what should I be thinking about in terms of my future

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:47.330
and where I need to be taking the business?

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:49.500
We talk about their industry

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:51.800
in 3 strategic imperatives.

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:54.170
The first one is digital customer engagement.

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:57.300
How do you improve the experience for the end user?

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:00.110
The second one is network and Cloud agility.

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:01.460
How do you leverage Cloud,

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:03.760
virtualize networks, et cetera?

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:06.230
And then the third one is enterprise transformation.

00:05:06.230 --> 00:05:07.890
And so it really kind of comes down

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:10.750
to accelerating delivery of value,

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:13.940
reducing operating costs and then increasing efficiency,

00:05:13.940 --> 00:05:15.970
and getting a deeper return on investment.

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:16.890
Absolutely.

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:20.330
I mean, the telcos are going to be the key enablers

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:24.600
for ensuring that the industries take advantage of the 5G.

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:26.400
This was a great conversation.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:27.830
I appreciate your expertise

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:29.260
and all the things that you've had to say

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:30.830
about the telco industry,

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:33.084
the world of 5G and Edge Computing.  Thank you.

00:05:33.084 --> 00:05:34.320
Thank you very much, Rob.

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:35.260
It's exciting.

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:37.213
Really enjoyed this conversation.

